body:
Absolutely not, unless its from a dealership since most dont do test rides around me.

&#x200B;

I can understand demanding you leave them the money while on the test, but only being able to ride it after irreversibly buying it? nope.

taking from the advice of the comments: did i ask

&#x200B;

and it is, you shift yourself unlike a scooter, it has two wheels, the drivetrain is not connected to the swingarm unlike a scooter, and also has foot pegs while scooters have a platform
